        "title": "Climate Zones and Biomes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Climate is the statistical description of atmospheric conditions over decades.\nThe Köppen classification is the canonical system — empirically derived from\nvegetation distributions in the 1900s, it remains the standard framework.\nEvery climate zone is the product of four interacting controls: latitude,\naltitude, continentality, and ocean currents. Biomes map onto climate zones\nwith remarkable fidelity — you can reconstruct one from the other."
    }
